-- title:
--   Conjugate cusp form with conjugated q-coefficients on Γ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number that is nonzero and let $k$ be an integer. The assertion is that there exists a map $\rho$ from the space $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ of cusp forms of weight $k$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(N)$ to itself such that for every cusp form $f \in S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ and every natural number $n$, the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $\rho f$ equals the complex conjugate of the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $f$; here the $n$-th $q$-coefficient of a form is, by definition, the coefficient of $q^n$ in its $q$-expansion taken with respect to the period $1$, and conjugation is the star ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{C}$. The existential statement asks only for a function between the underlying types: $\rho$ is not required to be additive, conjugate-linear, continuous or involutive, and no compatibility with Hecke operators is asserted. In particular the index $n = 0$ is included in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the classical stability of $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ under coefficientwise complex conjugation of $q$-expansions, realised by the antiholomorphic involution $f \mapsto \overline{f(-\bar z)}$. It is used in the arguments identifying Hecke eigenspaces attached to newforms inside Tate modules, where the existence of a conjugate form is needed to control the field generated by the Hecke eigenvalues.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_qCoeff_conj.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_qCoeff_conj (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (k : ℤ) :
    ∃ ρ : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) k → CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) k,
      ∀ (f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) k) (n : ℕ),
        ModularFormClass.qCoeff (ρ f) n = (starRingEnd ℂ) (ModularFormClass.qCoeff f n) := by sorry
